  "FINDINGS": {
    "sub_phase_template_trade_reference": "CORRECTED. The Trade lookup DOES exist on Sub-phase Template and is populated on 22 of 46 rows (24 pseudo-skill rows -- @office, @sub, @unassigned -- are deliberately null). On a trade-bearing row (SubPhaseNumber 1.2, \"Site Preparation\") the connector returns exactly the expected shape: \"Trade\":{\"@odata.type\":\"#Microsoft.Azure.Connectors.SharePoint.SPListExpandedReference\",\"Id\":6,\"Value\":\"Demolition\"} plus a sibling scalar \"Trade#Id\":6. CRITICAL BEHAVIOUR FOR TASKS 6-7: on a row where Trade is null (SubPhaseNumber 0.0), the SharePoint connector does not emit \"Trade\":null or \"Trade#Id\":null -- it OMITS both keys from the row entirely. Any expression must therefore treat the key as possibly ABSENT, not just possibly null. item()?['Trade']?['Id'] is still safe (the ?[] operator no-ops on a missing key and returns null/blank), but code must not assume the key is present, and any explicit key-existence check (e.g. contains()) must account for absence rather than null.",
    "task_template_subphase_reference": "CONFIRMED. Task Template rows carry SubPhase as {\"@odata.type\":\"#Microsoft.Azure.Connectors.SharePoint.SPListExpandedReference\",\"Id\":<int>,\"Value\":\"<title>\"} plus a sibling scalar \"SubPhase#Id\":<int>. Matches the expected shape exactly. Use item()?['SubPhase#Id'] or item()?['SubPhase']?['Id'] to join -- never Title/Value.",
    "work_calendar_date_column": "Key is \"Date\", a bare date-only string with no time component, e.g. \"2026-08-30\" (matches the DateOnly storage convention already documented in CLAUDE.md). Work Calendar rows also carry a \"Reason\" lookup ({Id, Value} + sibling \"Reason#Id\") that was not called out in the brief but is present and follows the same lookup-reference pattern as SubPhase and Trade."
  }
}